{
  "why": "The scorecard-analysis pivot is implemented TWICE — packages/domain/src/scorecard/analysis.ts (the server engine behind POST /scorecards/query) and apps/web/src/features/analyze-scorecards/model/analysis.ts (the client engine the studio actually runs). The duplication is load-bearing: the studio pivots an already-loaded list, and a round trip per filter toggle would make it unusable. What was NOT load-bearing was the lockstep — a comment in each file claiming the other is kept in step, which is a claim about another component and had no check. This file is that check: both engines answer the SAME question here, and each side's test asserts its own engine reproduces it. See docs/architecture/web-runtime-gap-census-spec.md.",
